<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Sickle</h1>
<p>Type of Weapon: Distanced Hand-to-hand.
</p><p>The sickle is another example of an agricultural tool used as a weapon or used as the basis for weapon development. Sickles, as an agricultural tool, were used for cutting grass, hay, and clearing foliage. Depending on the size of the sickle it could be wielded with one or two hands. While effective at slashing and getting around an opponent’s shield, this weapon wasn’t particularly useful for much else (except cutting grass).
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="In_Valhalla">In Valhalla</span></h2>
<p>In Valhalla the sickle is a weapon skill of its own, one of the swords (see <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>): one-handed, it slashes, it leans on dexterity, with some strength, and it is quick, as light weapons are. It is taught by the necromancers from guild level 10.
</p><p><br />
